  "result": "The 30-minute lesson on O3 is written, with a quiz ready to go. I haven't opened the lesson in a browser or run any file checks, so the length is only my estimate of about 3,500 words, inside the 2,700–6,750 range that fits 30 minutes.\n\n**Lesson:** `lessons/0001-context-and-memory-in-an-agent.html`\n\nIt covers three things, all using the makerspace assistant:\n- **The context window:** what is in it and why every token is paid for on every call.\n- **Between steps:** the program resends the whole history each step, which raises cost and leads to context rot. The fixes are clearing old tool results and compaction.\n- **Between sessions and retrieval:** the model keeps nothing unless your program saves it. Notes and records cover per-student facts like training status. Chunked retrieval covers long manuals, either up front or just in time through `search_manuals`.\n\nIt also has a recall warm-up on the agent loop, three figures, four practice checks with instant feedback, and a worked \"window, note or retrieval?\" sorting exercise with a faded one after it. The sources are Anthropic's context engineering post, the Claude docs page on context windows, and Anthropic's contextual retrieval article, all recorded in `RESOURCES.md`.\n\n**Quiz:** `quizzes/0002.json` has five fresh items (three multiple choice, one numeric, one short answer), with its key in `keys/0002.json`. Tell me when you want to take it.\n\n`NOTES.md` now records the lesson and quiz, and flags that you should watch for the belief that the model remembers across sessions on its own. Quiz 0001 is still ungraded.\n\nI can't point you to an online community for this lesson, so I suggested using the makerspace staff's real student questions as a test set. If you'd like a shorter or longer version, or any part explained another way, ask me in the chat.",
